", "image": "engenn6le03ob06re2img06.jpg", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"time": "100", "image": "engenn6le03ob06re2img06.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<span class =\"strong\">Peter</span>: Hey, Vanessa. What's up?<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Oh, I'm cooking up a storm because my family is coming over. So, I've gotta keep going, otherwise the meal won't be ready.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Peter</span>: Oh, I've got to make a meal too. John and Sandra are coming over. I've just gotta ask you some questions.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: OK."}, {"time": "17000", "image": "engenn6le03ob06re2img06.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<span class =\"strong\">Peter</span>: How much red wine should I put into a quart of tomato pasta sauce?<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Oh, not too much. 4 fluid ounces is plenty.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Peter</span>: My parents like espresso. How much coffee do I use?<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Three-quarters of an ounce is enough for a single shot.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Peter</span>: Thanks. So what're you making?"}, {"time": "35000", "image": "engenn6le03ob06re2img02.jpg", "id": 3, "text": "<span class =\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Oh, I'm making roasted chicken legs. My dad loves to grab those with his fingers. And grilled veggies, and tiramisu for dessert. <br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Peter</span>: I used to have tiramisu a lot. Well, I need to plan my meal. <br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Yup! And I'd better marinate the chicken before it goes in the oven. Good luck, Peter. <br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Peter</span>: You too, but I know you don't need any luck. Say hi to your family."}]}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "id": 2, "_data": []}]}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Vanessa: Dinner for Four"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Cooking Up a Storm"}, {"type": "position", "content": 6}, {"type": "origin", "content": "scholar > Looking to the Stars > Indira Gandhi"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 3}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Describe routines and regular activities in a wider range of social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn6le03ob06re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Wh questions to ask about quantities"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use \"<span class=\"strong\">How much</span>\" and \"<span class=\"strong\">How many</span>\" to ask about quantities. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use \"<span class=\"strong\">How much?</span>\" for uncountable nouns."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Structure: <br/><span class=\"strong\">How much</span> + <span class=\"italic\">uncountable noun</span> + auxiliary + subject + main verb + complement + ?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples:<br/><span class=\"strong\">How much</span> <span class=\"italic\">coffee</span> do I use? 4 fluid ounces is plenty.<br/> <span class=\"strong\">How much</span> <span class=\"italic\">red wine</span> should I put into a quart of tomato pasta sauce? Three-quarters of an ounce."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use \"<span class=\"strong\">How many?</span>\" for countable nouns."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Structure: <br/><span class=\"strong\">How many</span> + <span class=\"italic\">countable noun</span> + auxiliary + subject + main verb + complement + ?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples:<br/> <span class=\"strong\">How many</span> <span class=\"italic\">chicken legs</span> do you need? I need a lot! <span class=\"strong\">How many</span> <span class=\"italic\">peppers</span> are you going to use for the grilled veggies? I'm going to use only a few."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to come over "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to invite a friend to come over to your house for a visit"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Vanessa is cooking because her family is coming over for dinner."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le03ob06aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you hear/use"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "fluid ounce"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the measurement for fluids used in the U.S. and the U.K., which is equal to 30 ml. "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You should put in 4 fluid ounces of red wine into a quart of tomato pasta sauce."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le03ob06aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "espresso"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "strong tasting coffee made from fine grounds and water pushed with pressure."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Peter asked how much coffee he should use to make espresso."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le03ob06aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "single shot"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "one fluid ounce of espresso"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Three-quarters of an ounce is a good amount of coffee to use for a single shot of espresso."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le03ob06aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "grilled"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to cook food over a heated grill"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Vegetables cooked over a grill taste very different."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le03ob06aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to marinate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to put spices and/or a sauce on raw meat for a long time before cooking"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Vanessa wanted to marinate the chicken before it went in the oven."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le03ob06aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Research how to make a cappuccino."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read English barista web pages, or watch videos in English."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a dialogue where you show your partner how to make the cappuccino."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Include quantities and amounts in your instructions."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I research how to make a cappuccino. I read English instructions and watch videos in English."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a dialogue giving instructions on how to make the coffee."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I express quantities and amounts."}]}]}